OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen did Children's BBC become the
OL,7,Fumbrella name for all the BBC's output
OL,8,Ffor younger viewers?
OL,10,FIt's not as easy a question as you
OL,11,Fmight think.
OL,13,FThe Children's BBC strand was
OL,14,Fintroduced in September 1985 to replace
OL,15,Fnormal presentation but was confined to
OL,16,Fweekday afternoons.
OL,18,FPlay School, See Saw and Saturday
OL,19,Fmorning programmes were still linked by
OL,20,Fthe normal announcer with the standard
OL,21,Fident and graphics.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn fact, standard links returned to the
OL,7,Fafternoon for a brief period in the
OL,8,Fsummer of 1986 ` Children's BBC itself
OL,9,Fmoved to weekday mornings for the
OL,10,Fholidays.
OL,12,FThe first significant extension of the
OL,13,Fspecial branding came with the start of
OL,14,Fdaytime TV in October 1986.
OL,16,FChildren's BBC began a morning slot
OL,17,Faround Play School and, soon
OL,18,Fafterwards, the BBC micro ident started
OL,19,Fto be used around See Saw programmes
OL,20,Ftoo.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13103
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FOther strands gradually replaced
OL,7,Fstandard continuity ` But First This
OL,8,Fduring the summer school holidays, Now
OL,9,Fon Two on Sunday mornings.
OL,11,FYet until the early 90s, there were
OL,12,Fstill occasions when the globe was used
OL,13,Fbetween children's programmes.
OL,15,FThe last major example we've found is
OL,16,Ffrom September 1991.
OL,18,FRoger Maude ` by then one of the
OL,19,Flongest-serving and, by certain
OL,20,Fmeasures, old-fashioned of announcers `
OL,21,Flinked the Saturday morning line-up
OL,22,Fwith the standard BBC One graphics.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13104
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe fact the announcer was still needed
OL,7,Fon some occasions probably reflected
OL,8,Feconomics or wider editorial issues.
OL,10,FWas the money around to hire enough
OL,11,Fpresenters to cover all children's
OL,12,Foutput?
OL,14,FOn certain occasions was there even the
OL,15,Fneed? The lack of an in-vision
OL,16,Fpresenter before See Saw or Sunday's
OL,17,Frepeat of Play School was hardly
OL,18,Fconspicuous.
OL,20,FWhat is more surprising is the
OL,21,Finconsistent branding?
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13105
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FSometimes the Children's BBC graphics
OL,7,Fwere used on Saturday mornings by the
OL,8,Fregular announcer ` notably on the
OL,9,Fmorning in February 1991 when the new
OL,10,Fchannel idents were introduced.
OL,12,FYet the new globe made its debut before
OL,13,Fthe flagship children's programme Going
OL,14,FLive.
OL,16,FAnd, as I said, the standard idents
OL,17,Fpopped up all through Saturday's
OL,18,Fchildren's programmes on other
OL,19,Foccasions.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13106
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere were also exceptional occasions
OL,7,Fwhen normal presentation was used
OL,8,Faround afternoon children's programmes
OL,9,Finto the noughties. Occasionally
OL,10,Feditions of Blue Peter at Christmas and
OL,11,FNew Year were shown on days when there
OL,12,Fwere no other CBBC programmes.
OL,14,FAll of this is surprising in
OL,15,Fretrospect.
OL,17,FThe broom cupboard was popular with
OL,18,Fyoung viewers while it was soon
OL,19,Fforgotten that the name Children's BBC
OL,20,Fwas suspiciously similar to the name of
OL,21,Fits ITV rival launched two-and-a-half
OL,22,Fyears earlier.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,132,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13107
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F131A1786056988
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCInconsistent use of the
OL,4,CChildren's BBC brand in the 80s and 90s
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC ` both then and now ` has to
OL,7,Fthink carefully about resourcing. It is
OL,8,Funderstandable that the need for
OL,9,Fin-vision children's links did not
OL,10,Falways justify the cost.
OL,12,FBut you might have imagined someone
OL,13,Fsenior in Pres might have ruled on how
OL,14,Fother children's slots should have been
OL,15,Fbranded as early as 1987.
OL,17,FIf the regular announcer was being
OL,18,Fused, either they should have kept to
OL,19,Fthe standard idents or used the
OL,20,Fchildren's animation.
OL,23,APub: 02-Mar-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
